1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,590
A sound that keeps rising forever?

2
00:00:04,640 --> 00:00:06,360
Turn the sound on, but keep it low

3
00:00:06,410 --> 00:00:09,910
Listen all the way through
to hear how high it goes

4
00:00:09,960 --> 00:00:15,880
First, an ordinary staircase of notes

5
00:00:15,930 --> 00:00:17,450
Climb it, and you reach the top

6
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:21,220
Now listen to this one!

7
00:00:21,270 --> 00:00:25,220
It keeps going up…

8
00:00:25,270 --> 00:00:29,220
Still going up!

9
00:00:29,270 --> 00:00:32,220
But it never ends?!

10
00:00:32,270 --> 00:00:36,190
Actually, every 12 steps
it's back to the very first sound!

11
00:00:36,240 --> 00:00:38,360
It plays several notes at once,
each an octave apart

12
00:00:38,410 --> 00:00:42,630
They all step up together

13
00:00:42,680 --> 00:00:46,630
The note that gets too high
fades away

14
00:00:46,680 --> 00:00:51,130
while a new note sneaks in quietly
at the bottom

15
00:00:51,180 --> 00:00:55,100
So your ears only notice "going up"
and never catch the end

16
00:00:55,150 --> 00:00:57,350
This is called a "Shepard tone"

17
00:00:57,400 --> 00:00:59,450
NEXT: You can't lift your ring finger?
